---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title="Privacy: Hex & Hue"
  description="What Hex & Hue stores and sends: your progress stays on your device; no account needed."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Hex &amp; Hue is made to be played without handing over anything about yourself. There is no
      account to create and no sign-in.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your progress (levels, stars, coins, boosters, settings and which tips you have seen) is saved
      in your browser's storage on your own device. It is never sent to us. Clearing your browser's
      site data removes it, along with your analytics choice.
    </p>
    <h2>Offline files</h2>
    <p>
      To play offline, the game keeps a copy of its own files in your browser's cache. They contain
      no personal data.
    </p>
    <h2>Anonymous play stats (only if you agree)</h2>
    <p>
      If you allow it in the banner or in the game's Settings, Hex &amp; Hue counts a few anonymous
      events to learn which levels are too hard and where players stop: opening the game, starting,
      winning, losing or skipping a level (with its time and stars), boosters used, tips read, and
      how optional ads and the install offer ended.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        They are tied to a random id created on your device when you agree, never to your name,
        email or account (there is none). No cookies are used.
      </li>
      <li>They are sent to our analytics service (PostHog) and used only to improve the game.</li>
      <li>
        Nothing is collected until you agree. If your browser sends a "do not track" or Global
        Privacy Control signal, nothing is collected and we don't ask.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can change your mind any time in Settings; turning it off deletes the random id and
        anything not yet sent.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Optional ads</h2>
    <p>
      Rewarded ads only play when you choose to watch one. If an ad provider is used, it may process
      data under its own privacy policy, which we will link here.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is unclear, open an issue on the project's page or contact the developer.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
